</i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-23-email-desktop-dad31712.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:56.5%;top:31.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:35.5%;top:41.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.9%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.6%;top:22.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="email-backups-and-site-health-backups" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Backups</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The database is backed up every night, encrypted and test-restored on the spot. Kept: the last 7 nights and each Sunday of the last 4 weeks, with point-in-time recovery for the last week. Every night the retention keeps the backup storage under 70% of its free 10 GB.</li><li>Every Monday the newest backup is checked again: it must be under 30 hours old and restore cleanly.</li><li>A failed backup, or none for 30 hours, opens a site alert: an email (outside the quiet hours), a task and a line on To do. Tell your developer the same day.</li><li>Keep a copy of the backup key in the company password manager. Without it no backup can be read.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="email-backups-and-site-health-site-health-and-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Site health and alerts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, the Site health card at the bottom.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every 5 minutes the site checks itself: the home page, a car page, the sign-in page and the site&#39;s health check, and also emails, scheduled jobs, the nightly backup and Stripe payments.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hid