select app.guide_release_section('field', 'photo-shoots', 'chapter', 'a-return', 'A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.

## Shoot the listing photos

1. Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press **I have read this**.
2. The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot (or **From photos** to pick one you took). **Retake** to redo one.
4. An upload failed? Press **Send again**. Then press **Submit for listing**. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under **More outside photos** (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under **Other detail** (up to 20).

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg "phone; size: 390 730; pins: 1 89.7 34.2, 2 89.7 67.8, 3 29.0 97.3")

The steps at the top say where the listing is: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press **Remove** under that photo, then **Remove it**, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

> Tip: Keep other cars'' plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car''s plate before the listing goes live.
', 'Photo shoots', 'Shoot a listing''s photos in order and submit them.',
  'A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.

## Shoot the listing photos

1. Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press **I have read this**.
2. The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot (or **From photos** to pick one you took). **Retake** to redo one.
4. An upload failed? Press **Send again**. Then press **Submit for listing**. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under **More outside photos** (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under **Other detail** (up to 20).

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg "phone; size: 390 730; pins: 1 89.7 34.2, 2 89.7 67.8, 3 29.0 97.3")

The steps at the top say where the listing is: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press **Remove** under that photo, then **Remove it**, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

> Tip: Keep other cars'' plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car''s plate before the listing goes live.

**Add photos** takes up to 30 photos at once from the camera roll, in any order: each is sorted to its shot by itself. Take at least 10, the whole car outside from every side, then the inside. A watermark or caption at the edge of a photo is cut off by itself; a photo with one in the middle is kept off the site, so take your own photos rather than saving a dealer''s.',
  '<p class="gd-p">A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.</p><section class="gd-task" id="photo-shoots-shoot-the-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shoot the listing photos</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press <b class="gd-ui">I have read this</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot (or <b class="gd-ui">From photos</b> to pick one you took). <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> to redo one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An upload failed? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under <b class="gd-ui">More outside photos</b> (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under <b class="gd-ui">Other detail</b> (up to 20).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/730"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="730"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.7%;top:34.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.7%;top:67.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:97.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The steps at the top say where the listing is: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under that photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Keep other cars&#39; plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car&#39;s plate before the listing goes live.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> takes up to 30 photos at once from the camera roll, in any order: each is sorted to its shot by itself. Take at least 10, the whole car outside from every side, then the inside. A watermark or caption at the edge of a photo is cut off by itself; a photo with one in the middle is kept off the site, so take your own photos rather than saving a dealer&#39;s.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'quick-reference', 'reference', 'keeping-your-account-safe', '### Where things are

| Item | What it is for |
| --- | --- |
| **Home** | What needs you first, then each investment, returns, next payment |
| **Live sheets** | Your full schedule, the calculators and the Excel download |
| **Documents** | **Statements** (one per month; PDF, ZIP and CSV by year), **Documents to sign**, **Your files** (your agreement and schedules) |
| **Account** | Contact details, notices, transfers, two-step sign-in |

### Top tasks

1. *See what you earned:* **Documents** > **Statements**, then a month
2. *Keep a statement:* **Download PDF**
3. *A whole year:* **Documents** > **Statements**, then **Download a year**
4. *Paid monthly or reinvested:* **Send the notice**
5. *Change your bank account:* **Ask to change the bank account**
6. *Transfer an investment:* **Send the request**
7. *Protect your account:* **Set up two-step sign-in**

### If something goes wrong

| What you see | What to do |
| --- | --- |
| **A link says it expired** | Links in our emails work for 24 hours, once. Press **Send me a new link** on that page. |
| **"Error 1102" on a page** | A short limit on our web host. Reload the page. You are still signed in. |
| **"That email and password do not match an account."** | Check the address, or use **Set a new password** on the sign-in page. |
| **Asked for a 6-digit code** | Open your authenticator app. Lost your phone? Call us. |
